<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuri II of Vladimir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1189–1238</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Yuri Vsevolodovich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuri II Vsevolodovich was grand prince of Vladimir from 1212 to 1216 and again from 1218 to 1238, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vsevolod-the-big-nest">Vsevolod the Big Nest</a>. In 1221 he founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizhny-novgorod">Nizhny Novgorod</a> as a base against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>. When Batu's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> invaded in 1237–1238 he left Vladimir to gather troops, but the city was sacked and he was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-sit-river">Battle of the Sit River</a> on 4 March 1238.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuri-ii-of-vladimir.jpg" alt="Yuri II of Vladimir" width="320" height="550" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous Russian painter (1670s-1917) Public domain image (according to PD-Russia-expired) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Archangel_Cathedral_-_SW_column,_1st_lev.,_south_-_Georgy_Vsevolodovich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
